# Resolved, not authored.
.dart_tool/

# The lock. This repository is the application, which is the one place a tracked lock would be
# right — and it cannot be one here, because the same package is also the one every developer
# resolves beside the sibling checkouts. `dart pub get` rewrites the lock with whatever answered,
# so a tracked one holds path entries naming one machine's directories half the time and git refs
# the other half, and every resolution turns the other half into a change nobody made. What travels
# would be a disk layout rather than a set of versions, which is the opposite of what a lock is
# kept for. The refs in pubspec.yaml are what a build resolves against.
pubspec.lock

# The compiled binary. It is built by tool/build.dart rather than kept here.
build/

# The path override that points at the framework and plugin checkouts beside this one. Whoever
# has them writes their own; the git dependencies in pubspec.yaml are what everyone else
# resolves. Tracked, it would hand every clone a set of paths that are not there.
pubspec_overrides.yaml

# Agent instructions. Loaded from disk by whichever harness opens this repository, and never
# tracked: they are ours, and this repository is meant to be cloned and used by anybody.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
